##* {{quote-book|en|year=1928|author=George Bickerstaff|title=The mayor, and other folk
|passage=One other day after afternoon school, Mr. Percival came behind me and put his hand on me. "Let me see, what's your name? Which '''form''' are you in?{{nb...}}"}}
